      "source": "https://www.sulphurspringstx.org/general_information/history.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A railroad line from Mineola reached Sulphur Springs in 1872, sparking growth and bringing visitors to its mineral baths.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sulphurspringstx.org/general_information/history.php",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city’s first steam-powered factory opened in 1857 by the Bell brothers, marking the start of industrialization in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
